## What Is HealthSpring Medicare Advantage?

HealthSpring Medicare Advantage is a Medicare Advantage option that provides Medicare-covered healthcare benefits through a private health plan.

For someone seeking counseling, one of the most important parts of choosing or using a Medicare Advantage plan is understanding the **provider network**.

A provider network is the group of healthcare professionals and facilities that have a relationship with the health plan. Depending on the plan, using an in-network provider can affect what you pay and whether the service is covered under your plan's terms.

That is why simply finding a therapist who says they accept Medicare may not be enough. You should confirm that the therapist participates in **your specific HealthSpring Medicare Advantage plan**.

## Does Medicare Cover Therapy and Counseling?

Yes. Medicare Part B covers a wide range of outpatient mental health services.

Medicare.gov explains that outpatient mental health care can include counseling or psychotherapy provided individually, in groups, or in certain family settings. Covered services can include individual and group psychotherapy, family counseling when the primary purpose is treatment, psychiatric evaluations, medication management, diagnostic testing, and other behavioral health services.

Medicare also recognizes mental health counselors as professionals who may provide covered outpatient mental health services when applicable Medicare and state requirements are met.

Since Medicare Advantage plans administer Medicare benefits through private plans, members should check their specific plan for network and cost-sharing requirements.

## Is There a HealthSpring Medicare Advantage Therapist at Riaz Counseling?

The **2026 HealthSpring Texas and Oklahoma PPO provider directory lists Manahil Riaz as a Licensed Professional Counselor** under behavioral health providers. The directory includes a practice listing associated with Manahil Riaz in the Houston-area region.

