## Frequently Asked Questions

### Does Riaz Counseling accept HealthSpring Medicare Advantage?

The 2026 HealthSpring Texas and Oklahoma PPO provider directory lists **Manahil Riaz as a Licensed Professional Counselor** under behavioral health providers. Because Medicare Advantage coverage is plan-specific, confirm your exact HealthSpring plan and current benefits before scheduling treatment.

### Is Manahil Riaz listed as a HealthSpring provider?

Yes. Manahil Riaz appears in HealthSpring's 2026 Texas and Oklahoma PPO provider directory under the Licensed Professional Counselor category within behavioral health providers.

### Does Medicare Advantage cover therapy?

Medicare covers a range of outpatient mental health services, including individual and group psychotherapy and certain family counseling. With Medicare Advantage, the specific plan determines network arrangements and applicable cost-sharing, so members should verify their individual benefits.

### How do I find a counselor accepting HealthSpring?

Start with your HealthSpring provider directory and search for behavioral health professionals. Then confirm directly with the provider that they participate in your specific Medicare Advantage plan and ask about the service you need.

### Can I use HealthSpring for online therapy?

Medicare covers certain mental health services through telehealth and e-visits when applicable requirements are met. Your HealthSpring plan may have additional rules, so confirm telehealth coverage before scheduling a virtual appointment.

### What should I bring when contacting a therapist?

Have your insurance card available, including your member ID and plan information. It can also help to know what type of support you are looking for, whether you prefer in-person or online therapy, and whether you have any scheduling or location preferences.

### Will my HealthSpring plan cover every therapist at a counseling practice?

Not necessarily. Network participation can vary by plan and provider. Confirm the specific therapist and your exact plan rather than assuming that an entire practice is covered.

### Can I still get help if my preferred therapist is not in-network?

You may have other options. Ask your HealthSpring plan about additional in-network behavioral health providers and whether your plan provides any out-of-network coverage. You can also ask the counseling practice whether another participating provider may be available.

